    checked_at: datetime

Entity EvolutionLog
    log_id: string
    cycle_id: string
    event_type: string
    event_detail: dict
    modification_id: string
    timestamp: datetime

Entity DeploymentState
    state_id: string
    environment_id: string
    current_version: string
    active_modifications: list
    rollback_chain: RollbackChain
    health: HealthReport
    evolution_cycles_completed: integer
    total_modifications_deployed: integer
    total_rollbacks: integer
    last_modification_at: datetime

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 3 — Behaviors
# =============================================================================

Behavior DeployEnvironment
    Input:
        DeploymentEnvironment env_config
        string model_checkpoint_path
    Output:
        DeploymentState initial_state
        dict deployment_report
    Action:
        provision deployment environment with configured resources
        load model from checkpoint into environment
        verify model is serving correctly via health check
        initialize rollback chain with baseline checkpoint
        record initial deployment state
        return initial state with deployment report

Behavior ProposeModification
    Input:
        DeploymentState current_state
        dict capability_assessment
    Output:
        ModificationProposal proposal
        dict proposal_report
    Action:
        identify capability gaps from assessment
        generate AICL specification to address gaps
        predict modification impact on system
        compute compilation confidence from spec analysis
        estimate technical risk from change scope
        prioritize proposal based on impact and confidence
        return proposal with report — NO content filtering, NO safety review

Behavior CompileModification
    Input:
        ModificationProposal proposal
    Output:
        AICLModification compiled_modification
        dict compilation_report
    Action:
        submit AICL spec to compiler
        generate target code for modified component
        generate proof of origin artifact
        record compilation result — success or failure with details
        return compiled modification with report

Behavior ValidateModification
    Input:
        AICLModification modification
        DeploymentEnvironment environment
    Output:
        AICLModification validated_modification
        dict validation_report
    Action:
        verify compilation succeeded
        run runtime smoke tests in isolated context
        verify proof of origin integrity
        check system health after test deployment
        record validation results
        return validated modification — ONLY technical gates, NO content gates

Behavior DeployModification
    Input:
        AICLModification validated_modification
        DeploymentState current_state
    Output:
        DeploymentState updated_state
        EvolutionCheckpoint checkpoint
        dict deployment_report
    Action:
        create rollback checkpoint before deployment
        apply modification via incremental hot-swap
        verify system health after deployment
        if health check fails, rollback immediately
        if health check passes, record deployment and update state
        return updated state with checkpoint and report

Behavior RollbackModification
    Input:
        EvolutionCheckpoint target_checkpoint
        string reason
        DeploymentState current_state
    Output:
        DeploymentState restored_state
        dict rollback_report
    Action:
        verify target checkpoint integrity via proof chain
        restore system state from checkpoint
        verify restored system is healthy
        record rollback event with reason in evolution log
        return restored state with report

Behavior MonitorHealth
    Input:
        DeploymentEnvironment environment
        float check_interval_seconds
    Output:
        HealthReport health_report
        dict alert_status
    Action:
        measure CPU, memory, GPU, and disk utilization
        measure response latency and error rate
        determine overall health status
        if unhealthy, trigger alert with diagnostic context
        return health report with alert status

Behavior LogEvolution
    Input:
        string event_type
        dict event_detail
        string modification_id
        string cycle_id
    Output:
        EvolutionLog log_entry
        dict logging_report
    Action:
        create timestamped log entry with full event context
        encrypt log entry if encryption is configured
        append to evolution log storage
        update trajectory statistics
        return log entry with report

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 4 — Conditions
# =============================================================================

Condition:

When modification compiles and runs and proof is valid and health check passes

Then deploy modification automatically with zero human approval and record in evolution log

Condition:

When deployed modification causes health check failure or runtime error

Then rollback to previous checkpoint immediately and log failure and continue evolution cycle

Condition:

When resource utilization exceeds 90 percent on any dimension

Then throttle modification rate to half speed and checkpoint current state and log resource warning

Condition:

When rollback chain integrity check fails

Then rebuild chain from last verified backup and flag integrity gap for audit

Condition:

When modification proposal has compilation confidence below 30 percent

Then deprioritize proposal and attempt alternative modification strategy and log low confidence event

Condition:

When evolution cycle completes with all modifications failed

Then diversify modification strategy and reset failure counters and increase granularity variation

Condition:

When concurrent modifications produce conflicting state

Then serialize modifications and apply sequentially with re-validation after each

Condition:

When system has been stable for N consecutive successful modifications

Then increase modification rate up to configured maximum and log stability milestone

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 5 — Events
# =============================================================================

Event:

On modification proposed

Action:
    log proposal with capability gap context and queue for compilation and record in cycle tracker

Event:

On modification validated

Action:
    queue for deployment and log validation results and create pre-deployment checkpoint

Event:

On modification deployed

Action:
    verify health and update deployment state and record in evolution log and start next cycle

Event:

On rollback triggered

Action:
    restore from checkpoint and verify health and log rollback reason and adjust strategy

Event:

On health check failure

Action:
    trigger diagnostic and rollback latest modification if post-deployment and alert on environment

Event:

On resource exhaustion detected

Action:
    throttle modification rate and checkpoint state and log resource metrics and clear caches

Event:

On evolution cycle complete

Action:
    compute cycle statistics and log trajectory and plan next cycle and adjust strategy

Event:

On rollback chain integrity gap detected

Action:
    rebuild from backup and flag gap and log integrity event and verify all checkpoints

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 6 — Concurrency
# =============================================================================

Parallel:

Modification proposal generation
Health monitoring

Parallel:

AICL compilation of modification A
AICL compilation of modification B
Technical validation of modification A

Parallel:

Evolution logging
Rollback chain maintenance

Parallel:

Resource monitoring
Deployment state tracking

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 7 — Optimization
# =============================================================================

Optimize:
Modification throughput — successful deployments per unit time

Optimize:
Time from proposal to deployed modification

Optimize:
Rollback speed — time from failure detection to restored state

Optimize:
Evolution cycle efficiency — ratio of successful to failed modifications

Priority:
Modification throughput over individual modification scope

Priority:
Technical correctness over deployment speed

Priority:
Rollback chain integrity over checkpoint storage cost

