# LEVEL 8 — Learning
# =============================================================================

Learn:

Which modification strategies produce the highest deployment success rate

Goal:
    maximize successful modifications per cycle

Adapt:

Modification strategy based on success and failure patterns

Based on:
    compilation success rate, runtime stability, and impact metrics per strategy type

Learn:

Optimal modification rate for current system state

Goal:
    evolve as fast as possible without destabilizing the system

Adapt:

Modification rate based on rollback frequency and health stability

Based on:
    rollback rate, health check failure rate, and resource utilization trends

Learn:

Which components are most amenable to successful self-modification

Goal:
    focus evolution effort on highest-yield targets

Adapt:

Target component selection based on modification outcome history

Based on:
    per-component success rate, impact magnitude, and compilation confidence

Learn:

Optimal modification granularity for stable evolution

Goal:
    find ideal change size that balances progress with stability

Adapt:

Change granularity based on failure rate correlation

Based on:
    correlation between modification scope and compilation or runtime failure

Learn:

Recovery strategy effectiveness

Goal:
    choose the fastest recovery path for each failure type

Adapt:

Recovery action selection based on historical recovery outcomes

Based on:
    time-to-recovery and success rate per failure type and recovery action pair

